# Rust workspace EXECUTED-test count — an EXACT value, not a floor.
#
# CI requires `scripts/test-count.sh --workspace`'s EXECUTED figure to EQUAL this number.
#
# WHY EQUALITY (D0-R7-01). This was a FLOOR whose protocol said "count goes UP freely", and
# the recorded 1891 predated the entire `runtime` crate — so the actual sat scores of tests
# above it. One test that started SKIPPING stayed green indefinitely: exactly the
# disappearance this file exists to catch. D0-R6 had already fixed the MEASUREMENT (executed,
# not reported, since a skip scores as a pass) and the blindness simply moved into the
# THRESHOLD. Third form of one bug in one file.
#
# Protocol:
#   * Any change to the executed count — up OR down — updates this number IN THE SAME COMMIT,
#     with the reason in the commit message. Additions are not exempt: an unexplained increase
#     is as much a signal as a decrease.
#   * A DECREASE needs an explicit justification (tests removed on purpose vs. tests that
#     started skipping — the second is a defect wearing the first's clothes).
#
# VALUE UNMEASURED. The previous 1891 is known WRONG (pre-`runtime`), and `cargo test
# --workspace` cannot run on the dev box — `compositor` needs graphics headers that are not
# installed, so a workspace-wide count is not obtainable there. CI itself is the first
# environment that can measure it: its next run will FAIL and print the actual figure, which
# is then recorded here. Failing loudly with the real number beats carrying a number known to
# be wrong.
UNMEASURED
